# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for `make tsan`.
#
# The tsan target builds with clang + LLVM libomp and loads Archer, LLVM's
# OpenMP tool that tells TSan about OpenMP's barriers and task edges.  That
# removes the flood of false positives GCC's uninstrumented libgomp causes.
#
# What remains is one benign report inside libomp itself (its lazy
# pthread_mutex_init of an internal lock).  Only interceptor calls made FROM
# the OpenMP runtime are suppressed -- a race in our code still reports,
# because the racing access is in our frames.
called_from_lib:libomp.so
called_from_lib:libomp.so.5
called_from_lib:libomp.dylib
